comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-02T18:07:32.596Z","harness:claude-code","Scope evidence from the Codex review round 3 of PR 1654: dependency removal cannot address legacy blocker rows either. --dep-remove normalizes its selector id through normalizeItemReference and compares kinds literally. So a row stored with a short id (missing, normalized to pm-missing), an alias kind (depends_on, which canonicalizes to blocked_by everywhere else) or an external locator without source_kind in the selector (gh:org/repo#12, normalized to pm-gh:org/repo#12) fails with dependency_remove_no_match. Combined with this item's --unset blocked_by data loss, some blockers have no safe single-command removal. pm-urzubi's refusal therefore offers 'pm get <id> --fields blocked_by,dependencies' for them. Fixing this item should make removal selectors canonical (id normalization plus resolveCanonicalRelationshipKind) so recovery can advertise an executable removal again."
escape_class: production_defect
